# a Decimal and a Real are never mixed without a conversion: an operand of the wrong type is a compile error (D-080, D-110)
** spec: library/data-language.md#details-used-by-the-tests
** spec: semantics/errors.md (an operand of the wrong type is a compile error, never an error value)
primary aspect e74_decimal_real_mix is
  process main is
    print 1.5d + 2.5;
    print "not reached";
  return;
end e74_decimal_real_mix;
/*@expect
{
  "syntax_error": true,
  "exit": 65,
  "contains": [
    "operator + does not apply to Decimal and Real"
  ]
}
*/
